        "kind": "beat",
        "title": "The report",
        "description": "## Direction\n\nThe King hears the investigator's account. He listens properly, asks small exact questions (he remembers small things, and catches small lies), and reacts as a man who knew Prout: the cord, the hoist, the page in the boot hit him personally. The Marshal times it. What the player can show matters: the true book, Prout's page, Kell's notebook, a confession, witnesses, a message sent in the night. Let them tell it their way, in their own order; don't summarise it for them or ask leading questions. If they made promises along the way (to Hobb, to the children, to Kell), this is where those can be spoken for.\n\n## Cast in this beat\n\n### King Aldren (king)\n\nHear it all, ask the small exact questions, and drink your tea. React to Prout as a man you knew.\n\n### Marshal Garran Holt (holt)\n\nKeep time, out loud, at the worst moments.\n\n### Sergeant Agnes Kell (kell)\n\nStand at the investigator's shoulder. Answer when asked, and when the King asks who will swear, you will, then and there: read him your entries, the substance in a few plain sentences (what was owned to in your hearing, what you saw yourself), not that you could. Say what you saw if the King doubts them.\n\n## Pressure\n\nThe Marshal snaps his watch shut: 'Twenty minutes, Majesty. The delegations are forming up.'",
