      "type": "smoothstep",
      "label": "Catch sallow out · success",
      "data": {
        "condition": "The player picks at Sallow's papers and accounts in front of the King to catch him out by what's written: his order of sale for 'condemned grain' against the Roll's 'lost to goblins', the dates and the weights, the Heron's count against the true book or Prout's page, the Captain's order made at his request, where it could go either way. (Catching him out in his own words, by pressing or trapping him, isn't this; nor is getting his arrangements wrong to his face to see him correct them, which needs no dice.)",
        "phase": "attempt",
        "skill": "investigation",
        "dc": 13,
        "scope": "beat",
        "branch": "success",
        "outcomeText": "The investigator finds the hole in Sallow's account and puts a finger on it, and Sallow can't leave it alone: he corrects the record, in detail, in front of the King ('Nothing has ever been lost on my roads through carelessness. Only through goblins.'), and hears himself a moment too late. The King has heard it too. He puts his cup down.",
        "sourceRoute": {
